# Pin committed TypeScript build outputs to LF line endings.
#
# The D-02 freshness check rebuilds the .ts sources to a temp directory and
# compares the result byte-for-byte against the committed .js. If a Windows
# checkout stored those committed .js files with CRLF while a macOS/Linux CI
# rebuild emits LF, the comparison would fail on line endings alone — a false
# "stale build" signal that masks (or is mistaken for) real drift. Pinning the
# committed build outputs to LF here, together with tsconfig "newLine": "lf",
# keeps the freshness diff deterministic and meaningful across platforms.
install/*.js    text eol=lf
scripts/**/*.js text eol=lf
hooks/*.js      text eol=lf
